      "id": "OQ-1",
      "q": "decisions/lifecycle-artifact-scope.md names scripts/verify-process-fact-contract.mjs as the canonical mechanical-evidence location asserting the classifier accepts known lifecycle filenames (\"If any of these regress, the policy is broken and must be fixed before landing further DEV work\"). Neither checklist item mentions that script; CHK-002 instead adds a new, differently-located coverage-invariant smoke (packages/main/src/tasks/lifecycle-registry-contract.ts, wired into lattice validate). Does the new smoke fully substitute for that decisions-doc-designated verification surface for these four filenames, or should scripts/verify-process-fact-contract.mjs also be extended/asserted against them?",
      "evidence": "lifecycle-artifact-scope.md Verification section: \"Mechanical evidence lives in: scripts/verify-process-fact-contract.mjs — asserts the classifier accepts known lifecycle filenames plus evidence/transcript-diff.md and evidence/live-smoke-transcript.json under a story id... If any of these regress, the policy is broken and must be fixed before landing further DEV work.\" Grep-verified: scripts/verify-process-fact-contract.mjs currently has no assertion referencing acceptance-basis.json/pre-review-check.json/topology-critic-receipt.json/topology-exclusion-approvals.json membership in LATTICE_LIFECYCLE_ARTIFACT_FILENAMES (it does reference topology-critic-receipt.json/topology-exclusion-approvals.json only as signed-artifact names in an unrelated process-fact-registry check, not a classifier-membership check). CHK-002 title: \"Add a registry-coverage invariant smoke... Wire it into lattice validate the same way sibling smokes are wired\" — no mention of scripts/verify-process-fact-contract.mjs.",
      "sourcePointers": [
        "docs/requirements/decisions/lifecycle-artifact-scope.md#verification",
        "scripts/verify-process-fact-contract.mjs",
        "packages/main/src/tasks/lifecycle-registry-contract.ts"
      ],
      "resolution": "Both locations get evidence, split by what each does best. scripts/verify-process-fact-contract.mjs (the location lifecycle-artifact-scope.md #Verification names as canonical for classifier-accepts-known-filenames evidence) gains a source-level assertion, in its existing extractConstInitializer style, that the four newly registered filenames are present in the LATTICE_LIFECYCLE_ARTIFACT_FILENAMES initializer, so the doc claim stays mechanically true. The richer runtime invariant (classifyLifecycleArtifact returns kind=lifecycle for the four paths, negative controls, store.ts write-set derivation with named exemption and named-divergence failure) lives in packages/main/src/tasks/lifecycle-registry-contract.ts, which is the dedicated registry-consistency contract and can import the compiled module for runtime behavior, which a source-text .mjs checker cannot do idiomatically. The doc Verification list is an evidence inventory, not an exclusivity rule; it will be updated with one bullet naming the new registry-contract evidence so the inventory stays accurate. plan.md CHK-002 section updated to reflect the split.",
      "resolvedAt": "2026-07-24T00:18:51.373Z"
    }
  ]
